The expected delegation should look roughly like:

Main Agent
    │
    ├── task
    │     ↓
    │   risk-analyst
    │     ↓
    │   Risk report
    │
    └── task
          ↓
        budget-planner
          ↓
        Budget report

          ↓
     Main Agent
          ↓
   Combined recommendation

-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Here we see two task calls similar to:

Tool Name: task

subagent_type: risk-analyst
description: Analyse the dashboard launch risks...

and:

Tool Name: task

subagent_type: budget-planner
description: Prepare a budget allocation for €20,000...

Deep Agents automatically adds the task tool when we provide subagents,
and the main agent uses each subagent's name and description to choose the appropriate specialist.
By default, these declarative subagents operate with isolated context.


The key Lesson 2 concept is:
Lesson 1:
Main Agent → One Specialist

Lesson 2:
Main Agent
   ├── Specialist A
   ├── Specialist B
   └── potentially more specialists